Normal
  h j k l       move left/down/up/right (arrow keys also work)
  0 $ w b e     line and word motions
  g G %         file start/end and matching brace
  N motion      count prefix repeats a motion (also n, N, u, U)
  N g / N G     go to line N
  N d           delete N lines
  i I a A       enter Insert mode
  o O           open line below/above
  x dd yy p     delete, delete line, yank line, paste
  d motion      delete over the next motion
  v V           character/line Visual mode
  u U           undo/redo (Ctrl-R also redoes)
  / n N         search, next match, previous match
  :             Command mode
  r             replace with the next typed key (Escape cancels)
  Ctrl-N        toggle file explorer (Escape closes it)
  Ctrl-P        toggle the recent-file list (Escape closes it)
  Ctrl-Z        suspend to the shell; fg returns
  space n       leader mapping for Ctrl-N
  space r       leader mapping for Ctrl-P
  Ctrl-M        toggle markdown display (Enter is the same key)
  s char        EasyMotion jump to any char on screen (both directions)
  t char        EasyMotion jump just before the next char (forward only)
  *             search the word under the cursor, highlight every match
  space i       leader mapping for *
  space o       leader mapping for :nohl
  space l       leader mapping for :set list!
  space f       leader mapping for :autoformat
  Ctrl-F Ctrl-B forward/back one screen (a count multiplies all six)
  Ctrl-D Ctrl-U forward/back half a screen
  Ctrl-E Ctrl-Y scroll one line, leaving the cursor where it is
  Ctrl-A Ctrl-X add one to / take one off the number at or after the cursor
  Ctrl-G        report the file, its length and the position in it
  Ctrl-L        redraw the screen and clear the message line
  Ctrl-V        blockwise Visual mode
  Ctrl-W        vim's window prefix; Cano has no splits and says so

Mouse
  click         move the cursor (gutter goes to the line start)
  click+drag    select in Visual mode
  wheel         scroll three lines
  scrollbar     click or drag the bar on the right to scroll
  click in list select an entry; click it again to open

Insert
  Escape        return to Normal
  arrows        move and split insertion history
  Tab           insert the configured indentation
  Backspace     delete byte before cursor
  Ctrl-H        the same as Backspace
  Enter         newline plus brace-depth indentation
  Ctrl-W        delete the word before the cursor
  Ctrl-U        delete back to the first non-blank; again for the indent
  Ctrl-T Ctrl-D indent / unindent the current line one shiftwidth
  Ctrl-N Ctrl-P complete the word being typed from the buffer, either way
  Ctrl-O        run one Normal-mode command, then carry on typing

Visual
  motions       extend selection (h j k l 0 $ w b e g G % and arrows)
  s char        extend the selection to an EasyMotion label
  d/x y         delete or yank
  > <           indent or unindent selected rows
  =             autoformat the selected lines
  <c-e> space e toggle line comments over the selected lines
  Ctrl-V        turn the selection into a rectangle, or leave Visual mode

Command and Search
  up/down       walk the history for that prompt
  Ctrl-F        open that history as a list (j/k, Enter runs, Escape closes)
  Ctrl-C        abandon the line
